</style>
<h2>Asobi 0.2 (build 203)</h2>
<p><b>Optional watermark for reviewer invites</b>, plus a round of fixes from a full bug audit.</p>
<ul>
<li><b>Watermark their copy</b> — a checkbox in Invite a Reviewer…. Tiles a faint diagonal identity (their name, by default) across the picture on their copy: viewport, frame grabs and exports alike. Carried in the signed invite, so it can't be quietly stripped. Off by default — it deters and traces, it doesn't prevent.</li>
<li><b>Review Speed no longer compounds through save/load.</b> A clip saved at half speed reopened at quarter speed, and halved again on every cycle. Fixed.</li>
<li><b>Timecode, SRT exports and burned-in movies now use the media's own rate while a clip is retimed</b> — subtitles landed in the wrong place and exports played at the review speed.</li>
<li>A slate inserted into an empty timeline now loads properly; a slate that fails to build says so instead of silently doing nothing.</li>
<li>Reconnecting relay sessions no longer leak network resources per attempt, and a finished shared session no longer leaves ghost cursors for the next one.</li>
</ul>
]]></description>
